Overlay patch 0041 (D24): REAL-TIME TICK CATCH-UP + the SOH_PACE probe.
Port of Shipwright-ios 0065 (D-084).

THE MECHANISM. GameEngine::ProcessGfxCommands (Starship's equivalent of SoH's
Graph_ProcessGfxCommands) runs once per game tick and renders
fps / tickHz interpolated frames for it (tickHz = 60 / gVIsPerFrame: 30 Hz in
most of SF64, so 4 frames per tick at 120 Hz). Every frame blocks on the
display and nothing looks at the wall clock, so a frame that misses its vsync
STRETCHES THE TICK: one 16.7 ms frame among four 8.3 ms ones makes a 30 Hz
tick 41.7 ms = 24 Hz = the game 20 % slow-motion. (Starship's audio self-pumps
on its own thread since overlay 0028, so its music tempo follows the audio
clock rather than the tick -- unlike SoH -- but gameplay, enemy timing and
the sync of SFX to it still follow the tick.)

THE FIX (same as SoH). Keep a debt: real time elapsed minus ticks x tick
period, clamped to [0, one tick]; a stall over 250 ms resets it so the game
never fast-forwards through a pause. While the debt is at least one frame
period, drop that many of THIS tick's EARLIEST interpolated frames (never the
last, the tick's real state) by advancing ProcessGfxCommands' `time`
accumulator before its build loop -- the dropped frames' interpolation is
never computed. gSohIos.TickCatchup (default 1) is the A/B switch; 3D
(visionOS immersive) is left alone (the compositor paces it). The gfx
debugger override still runs after.

THE PROBE (no behaviour change): one `SOH_PACE` line per 10 s, beside
SOH_PERF: tick wall p50/p95/max + tps, and each 2D frame split into
  wait  -- inside SetupScreenFramebuffer (nextDrawable / background park)
  busy  -- drawable acquired -> SwapBuffersBegin: the game thread's CPU work
  sleep -- LUS's SyncFramerateWithTime nanosleep pacer
plus frames skipped, ticks that skipped, debt, thermal and power state
(shell SohIos_PowerState: Low Power Mode caps the panel at 60 Hz).
gSohIos.PaceStressMs (default 0, test instrument) busy-waits that many ms per
frame so the catch-up can be proven on a simulator.

Code lives in new files src/port/SohIosPace.{h,cpp} (source of truth:
overlay/assets/probe/); the vendor hunks are call sites only. Every hunk keeps
clear of earlier patches' hunks + contexts so the series stays reversible.
Generate against a vendor tree with 0001..0040 applied (0041 applied or not).

--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/port/SohIosPace.h
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+// SOH_IOS (overlay 0041, D24): pace probe + real-time tick catch-up -- shared
+// state for the later probes (0042 spike probe, 0043 menu split). iOS only.
+#pragma once
+#ifdef __IOS__
+#include <chrono>
+
+namespace SohIosPace {
+using Clock = std::chrono::steady_clock;
+// Pace seams of the most recent 2D frame (game thread only):
+//   gDrawBegin  -> gDrawEnd    nextDrawable (SetupScreenFramebuffer)
+//   gDrawEnd    -> gSleepBegin the frame's CPU work
+//   gSleepBegin -> ...         LUS's SyncFramerateWithTime nanosleep pacer
+extern Clock::time_point gDrawBegin, gDrawEnd, gSleepBegin;
+// Interpolation fps of the current tick (frame period = 1000 / gFps ms).
+extern int gFps;
+inline double Ms(Clock::time_point a, Clock::time_point b) {
+    return std::chrono::duration<double, std::milli>(b - a).count();
+}
+inline bool Set(Clock::time_point t) {
+    return t.time_since_epoch().count() != 0;
+}
+} // namespace SohIosPace
+
+extern "C" {
+// Called by GameEngine::ProcessGfxCommands once per game tick, before the
+// interpolated frames are built: returns how many of this tick's EARLIEST
+// frames to drop (0..frames-1) and feeds the SOH_PACE report.
+int SohIos_TickCatchup(int fps, int tickHz, int frames);
+void SohIos_PaceDrawableBegin(void);
+void SohIos_PaceDrawableEnd(void);
+void SohIos_PaceSleepBegin(void);
+void SohIos_PaceSleepEnd(void);
+int SohIos_ThermalState(void);
+int SohIos_PowerState(void); // shell: 1 LPM, 2 charging, 4 full, 8 unknown
+extern volatile int gSoh3DMode;
+}
+#endif
